    "description": "# Oddwater\n\nA living freshwater aquarium with a slightly impossible imagination. Tend a planted community tank, get to know its residents, and awaken three surreal dreams.\n\nWatch neon tetras and harlequin rasboras school through the plants, peppered corys forage over the gravel, and a pearl gourami patrol the water. Shrimp browse the substrate, snails graze the glass, and tiny freshwater insects explore the shallows.\n\nOpen the **keeper’s notebook** to choose foods, improve filtration and aeration, adjust the light cycle, grow plants from cuttings, and raise juveniles in a sheltered nursery. Name your fish, build their trust, complete the field guide, and work through ongoing keeper projects. Arrange moss, leaf litter and pebble refuges to support a living clean-up crew. Raise cherry shrimp, watch their young grow, and record discoveries from meals, nights and moults. Your aquarium’s history and progress save automatically.\n\nDrag to orbit, scroll to zoom, and click a resident to inspect it. On phones, use the zoom buttons, Notebook and Tank notes. Press **J** for the notebook or use the gear button for graphics, sound, controls and accessibility.\n\nChoose **Ultra** for the richest water, reflections, caustics and fish textures. Turn Sound on for soft aquarium ambience and an original instrumental soundtrack.",
